Bound the SBR high-band patches.

sbr_generate_high_freq.cpp built the patches from the master table
without checking it:
- a master table with tiny bands made more than MAX_NUM_PATCHES patches,
  written past targetStartBand[] and then past the patch borders of
  sbr_create_limiter_bands() (stack overflow); the construction stops at
  MAX_NUM_PATCHES.
- an empty patch looped with an unchanged state when goalSb was already
  usb (a hang, libFuzzer timeout); it now stops the construction.
- the LPC analysis ran up to v_k_master[0], past the 32 QMF bands of the
  source buffers.
- the HQ coefficients shifted by 2 + shift_factor, negative when the
  quotient overflows; the overflow flag already discards them, so they
  are set to 0 first.

Regression input: tools/aacdec-fuzz/regressions/t169-sbr-patch-count.bin.

